<title>INDIA: India Arvind 96/97 1st half net up.</title>
<headline>India Arvind 96/97 1st half net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    581.0	vs	502.7</p>
<p>    Net sales	   3,907.0	vs    3,101.9</p>
<p>    Shr  (in rupees) *   11.64     vs	 10.07</p>
<p>    Other income	  207.2	vs	367.2</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 3,156.0	vs    2,693.1</p>
<p>    Interest costs	 61.7	vs	 42.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  275.5	vs	230.5</p>
<p>    Tax			40.0	vs	Nil</p>
<p>    Export earnings   1,752.6	vs    1,552.1</p>
<p>* EPS figure is annualised.</p>
<p>Note: Arvind Mills, part of the Lalbhai Group, is India'a leading producer of denim fabrics and a major exporter. It said Ankur Textiles, a division of the company, was sold on May 18, 1996. A loss of 19.6 million rupees on account of loss on sale of the unit is included in expenditure. Figures for year ago period have been regrouped wherever necessary, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
